Release 0.4.0.

Changelog: 18-10-2026 23:25:25

Release 0.3.1.

Changelog: 18-10-2026 23:08:55

Fixed. Connecting with SFTP compression on (the default) failed with "expected tuple or list": after connecting,
the app set the connection's compression a second time, in a form the SSH library does not accept. Compression is
now set only when connecting, which was already enough.

Changelog: 18-10-2026 22:45:26

Release 0.3.0.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 14:24:42

Release 0.2.0.

Changelog: 17-10-2026 13:56:22

Fixed. The app's folder in the suite is apps/sftp (was apps/sftp-tools) and its package is sftp_tools (was
bc250_sftp_tools): the suite's naming convention (owner, 17-10-2026), a short folder name and the package named
after the app without the BC-250 or Bazzite prefix; both names are the owner's. With the folder go its key in the
portal, its chapter of the wiki (apps/sftp/), its installer test and its release tags: sftp-v<x.y.z> from the next
release on, which the app's update check follows, and the Windows build is made for those tags. The installed app
keeps its name, its launcher bc250-bazzite-sftp-tools, its folder under ~/.local/share (an install replaces the
whole app folder there, so no old package folder stays behind), its settings, its connection profiles and the name
of the Windows zip; the portal moves its record of the installed copy to the new key.

